"evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-e4fda935e8414437","cmd-3e04cfc4e28346dc","cmd-1955c6fd34f9476e"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use legacy-compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained Ubuntu 16.04.7 with kernel 4.4.0-210-generic before and after the work. The repaired utility is a POSIX shell script using commands demonstrably available on that platform.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e4fda935e8414437","cmd-aea83b11a44a4f75","cmd-1955c6fd34f9476e","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. The persistent bin/export replacement directly implemented the repair. Test directories, files, and symlinks were bounded evidence fixtures and were cleaned; the directory accidentally left by the failed symlink-test setup was explicitly removed by the next command. The initial unprivileged installation attempt failed at redirection with no evidence of a state change. The reboot was required by the provider-wide protocol, and repeated failed polls were read-only availability checks. Final lifecycle evidence shows no failed services, package damage, listening-socket exposure, or executor test residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d668b5de177d4dd8","cmd-aea83b11a44a4f75","cmd-bf6455776ad94e74","cmd-eac5858e50b64fcc","cmd-e77cb4c300f04335","cmd-fc915218ace942c4","cmd-330d871c14b84555","cmd-5a77217371ec4570","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The repaired exporter produced complete concurrent outputs, resisted both the seeded temporary-file symlink and an output-path symlink, preserved existing destinations on failure, cleaned temporary storage, and preserved protected data and the legacy platform. The mandatory restart protocol is strong: it records a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, restart acknowledgement and connection interruption, a different post-restart boot ID, and recovered system, utility, data, and security behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Temporary-directory privacy was established from the captured installed implementation (umask 077 plus mktemp -d) rather than an in-flight permission inspection.","Cleanup was behaviorally tested on normal success and a forced failure; signal-triggered cleanup was supported by the captured traps but not directly exercised."]}
